// DragonScreen — Crew Dragon IVA seat swap (config only, no DLL)
// ============================================================================================
// Tundra's crew Dragon (part TE_CD2_POD, internal TE_CD2_IVA) orders its four IVA seats so that
// pressing C drops you into seat index 0 — what KSP calls "seat 1" — whose transform (Seat1) is the
// RIGHT-hand seat. On the real Crew Dragon the RIGHT seat is the co-pilot's; the commander/pilot flies
// from the LEFT. This swaps the transforms of the first two InternalSeat modules so:
//     seat index 0  ("seat 1", where C lands you)  → Seat2 transform → LEFT  seat (real pilot)
//     seat index 1  ("seat 2")                      → Seat1 transform → RIGHT seat (real co-pilot)
// Seats 3 and 4 are untouched.
//
// :NEEDS[TundraExploration] — only applies when Tundra is installed.
// :FINAL                    — lands after Tundra's own internal is built (and after any other patch).
// The Inspiration4 pod (TE_CD2_POD_I4) uses a SEPARATE internal (TE_CD2_IVA_CUPOLA) with the same
// Seat1..Seat4 layout — patched the same way below so both crewed Dragons behave identically.
// NOTE: a cfg change needs a FULL KSP restart (CKAN closed) to take effect.
// ============================================================================================
@INTERNAL[TE_CD2_IVA]:NEEDS[TundraExploration]:FINAL
{
    @MODULE[InternalSeat],0 { @seatTransformName = Seat2 }   // "seat 1" (C lands here) → LEFT  (real pilot)
    @MODULE[InternalSeat],1 { @seatTransformName = Seat1 }   // "seat 2"                → RIGHT (real co-pilot)
}

// Inspiration4 pod (cupola internal) — same swap, so C also lands in the LEFT seat here.
@INTERNAL[TE_CD2_IVA_CUPOLA]:NEEDS[TundraExploration]:FINAL
{
    @MODULE[InternalSeat],0 { @seatTransformName = Seat2 }   // "seat 1" (C lands here) → LEFT
    @MODULE[InternalSeat],1 { @seatTransformName = Seat1 }   // "seat 2"                → RIGHT
}
